# The build context is everything NOT listed here, so this file is what keeps
# `docker build` at ~10 MB instead of ~11 GB.

# The archive itself (11 GB) and the server's working state. Both arrive at
# runtime through the ./data volume mount -- never baked into the image.
data/
state/

# Host-side working directories: cards staged for `make import`, the legacy
# pre-`data/` output folder, run logs.
import/
cards/
logs/

# The macOS pngquant binary. Excluding it is what makes the image work:
# PngWriter._resolve_pngquant falls back to `shutil.which("pngquant")` when the
# configured path is missing, so the Linux one installed by apt wins. Ship the
# Mach-O binary and every card build would fail on it.
aspect/pngquant

# Local configuration. Correctness, not size -- config.py reads ROOT/.env, and
# a developer's .env may set an ARCHIVE_DIR override.
.env

# The image is the server only; tests, scripts and docs stay on the host (see
# README, "What is in the image").
#
# The userscript *sources* are the exception: the server compiles a configured
# bridge from them for Settings -> Userscripts (aspect/userscripts.py), which is
# the only install path a container user has. Only src_jai/ and src_saucepan/
# are COPYd in, so the tests and the checked-in bundles below never ship.
tests/
scripts/
userscript/tests/
userscript/package.json
userscript/*.user.js
docs/
example.json

# The React client's build inputs stay out of the context; its *output* does
# not come from the context at all -- the frontend-builder stage produces it
# from frontend/ source, which must therefore NOT be excluded here. Excluding
# node_modules is what keeps this file doing its job (see the header): it is
# hundreds of MB of the largest kind of small file.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/coverage/
frontend/openapi.json

# Build/tooling detritus.
.venv/
.git/
.github/
.claude/
node_modules/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.py[co]
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
compose.yaml
Makefile
